# UP Flow security

- Never store the Up **Personal Access Token** in plaintext files, env checked into git, or client-only `localStorage`. Use Tauri + OS keychain (`keyring`) as in `apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs`.
- Never disable TLS verification (`VERIFY_NONE`, insecure HTTP client flags). All Up traffic must use verified HTTPS (`rustls` / system trust).
- Do not log tokens, webhook `secretKey`, or full API responses in production builds.
- Webhook handlers must verify `X-Up-Authenticity-Signature` (SHA-256 HMAC of raw body) per [Up API docs](https://developer.up.com.au/).
